+export const FIXTURES = {
+  "nasa": {
+    "html": "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Worlds beyond our Sun · research notebook</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"A locally authored demonstration inspired by NASA's public exoplanet and Webb research topics.\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"ScholarlyArticle\",\"name\":\"Worlds beyond our Sun\"}</script></head><body><main>\n<p>LOCAL AUTHORED DEMO · This is an original teaching fixture, not a live NASA page or a NASA announcement. Follow the source links to read current public research.</p>\n<h1>Worlds beyond our Sun</h1>\n<p>An exoplanet is a planet orbiting a star beyond our solar system. Researchers compare many kinds of evidence: a star's changing brightness, its slight wobble, and the light that passes through a planet's atmosphere.</p>\n<h2>Reading an atmosphere with Webb</h2>\n<p>When a planet crosses its star, a small fraction of starlight can filter through the planet's atmosphere. Webb's infrared instruments help scientists study patterns in that light. A spectral feature is a clue to interpret alongside uncertainty, clouds, chemistry, and repeated observations.</p>\n<p>Use this notebook to select a passage, invite a clearly labeled local simulated companion, and save a cited artifact. No live researcher or external AI service is connected.</p>\n<h2>Keep the evidence close</h2>\n<p>Ask what was measured, which model connects the measurement to a claim, and what another observation could rule out. This fixture reports no new discovery and supplies no invented dates, planet counts, or mission results.</p>\n<nav><a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanets/\">Explore NASA's exoplanet science</a><a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/webb/\">Read about the Webb mission</a></nav>\n</main></body></html>\n",
+    "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanets/",
+    "sha256": "8af440b4a4c9cd64109f1a2cb0627add0a890ad2696caeb4b1307d17b3314470"
+  },
+  "restaurant": {
+    "html": "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Juniper Table · a seasonal menu</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Local authored restaurant demonstration. Menu and prices are fictional.\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Restaurant\",\"name\":\"Juniper Table\",\"servesCuisine\":\"Seasonal vegetables\"}</script></head><body><main>\n<p>LOCAL AUTHORED DEMO · Juniper Table is a fictional restaurant. These illustrative dishes, hours, and prices are not a live offer. This surface cannot place orders or make reservations.</p>\n<h1>At the table, in season</h1>\n<p>A small neighborhood kitchen imagined around vegetables, warm bread, and unhurried conversation. The menu changes with the fictional harvest; ask a real restaurant directly about ingredients and allergens.</p>\n<h2>Tonight's menu</h2>\n<p>Roasted squash · tahini yogurt, toasted seeds, garden herbs · $18. Mushroom barley · slow-cooked grains, browned butter, parsley · $24. Pear and almond cake · cultured cream · $11. All prices are illustrative.</p>\n<h2>Plan a visit</h2>\n<p>Illustrative service: Wednesday through Sunday, 5–9 pm. The source contains a reservation affordance, but this interpretation only detects it. No booking request, payment, or personal information is sent.</p>\n<form action=\"https://restaurant.example/reservations\" method=\"post\" aria-label=\"Reservation request\"><label>Preferred evening <input name=\"date\" type=\"date\"></label><button type=\"submit\">Request a table</button></form>\n<a href=\"https://restaurant.example/menu\">View the fictional source menu</a>\n</main></body></html>\n",
+    "url": "https://example.com/seasonal-menu",
+    "sha256": "f05cb6bdf8484c74bb8bd46f628ac4ba65f0a1045573d6f17b4ac811cbc131a1"
+  },
+  "github": {
+    "html": "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>netscape-infinite / field-notebook · repository study</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Local authored repository navigation demo, not a fetched GitHub repository.\"><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"SoftwareSourceCode\",\"name\":\"field-notebook\",\"programmingLanguage\":\"TypeScript\"}</script></head><body><main>\n<p>LOCAL AUTHORED DEMO · This repository listing and README are fictional teaching material. They are not a live GitHub snapshot and make no claim about a repository's current files, commits, contributors, or license.</p>\n<h1>field-notebook</h1>\n<p>A small imagined TypeScript project for keeping research passages with their citations. The repository view preserves file navigation and provenance while keeping execution, installation, and writes outside this demonstration.</p>\n<h2>Files and reading paths</h2>\n<p>Start with README.md for the project question, then follow the source module and its test. The links illustrate repository navigation; opening one is an explicit external action and may lead to an unavailable fictional resource.</p>\n<nav><a href=\"https://github.com/netscape-infinite/field-notebook/blob/main/README.md\">README.md · project introduction</a><a href=\"https://github.com/netscape-infinite/field-notebook/blob/main/src/notebook.ts\">src/notebook.ts · citation model</a><a href=\"https://github.com/netscape-infinite/field-notebook/blob/main/tests/notebook.test.ts\">tests/notebook.test.ts · behavior</a></nav>\n<h2>README · preserve the chain of evidence</h2>\n<p>A saved artifact should carry its selected passage, source address, content hash, and whether the source was a fixture or fetched public HTML. A link to code is evidence of navigation, not permission to run the code.</p>\n</main></body></html>\n",
+    "url": "https://github.com/example/morphogenesis-notebook",
